   shows the dialogue it has just answered), and a moment of listening is not being called on again.
 
+* **Latching (F71, ``Config.latch``; with silent claims).** While it only listens the mind does not read anew at
+  every context it has no record of whatever came before. A run of items (an utterance, a sentence) is one thought:
+  it is sought from the run's beginning until it claims something, followed to the next context as long as what
+  it claimed is what was then heard, and it reaches further with every claim that held (the window of F70 is that
+  many steps wider); where a claim of it failed, the thought is let go and the mind only listens until the next
+  run begins.
+
 Nothing here names a word, a frame or a domain; no number is chosen (one experience per settled claim, the core's
 k, the line the mind already speaks at). ``report`` says what the mind has learned about its own ways and where its
 last faults were.
